[{:db/id 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124863 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121778 :answer-field/correct 17592186121782 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79349" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nIII. $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=5$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e9f16a7-f4b2-5dc6-b4b7-1d7e51e453fc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e9f16a7-f4b2-5dc6-b4b7-1d7e51e453fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9f16a7-f4b2-5dc6-b4b7-1d7e51e453fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7c2003c1-be5a-5ec0-8d3f-914e8ee86a4a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75acd049-7010-5a98-8813-f29e53e8c979" "answer-46090913-fe8a-53d8-a2e2-1edec9407dcb" "answer-293235d4-a2f2-5777-a667-1540f003765f" "answer-596e4b3c-1fd0-573a-82a9-d1617135d478" "answer-7c2003c1-be5a-5ec0-8d3f-914e8ee86a4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75acd049-7010-5a98-8813-f29e53e8c979" :answer/id #uuid "75acd049-7010-5a98-8813-f29e53e8c979" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46090913-fe8a-53d8-a2e2-1edec9407dcb" :answer/id #uuid "46090913-fe8a-53d8-a2e2-1edec9407dcb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-293235d4-a2f2-5777-a667-1540f003765f" :answer/id #uuid "293235d4-a2f2-5777-a667-1540f003765f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-596e4b3c-1fd0-573a-82a9-d1617135d478" :answer/id #uuid "596e4b3c-1fd0-573a-82a9-d1617135d478" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c2003c1-be5a-5ec0-8d3f-914e8ee86a4a" :answer/id #uuid "7c2003c1-be5a-5ec0-8d3f-914e8ee86a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186272239 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-26e5acff-8db9-5e5d-9122-36baf139baac" :activity/id #uuid "26e5acff-8db9-5e5d-9122-36baf139baac" :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049340 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["s